I decided to try my first Yeoman under Lethe on slashem.crash-
override.net this time, and I ascended on my first try.

This makes two consecutive Slashem Lethe ascensions.

In minetown, I was attacked by a kobold warrior, who turned out to be
a gnome with a /WoPoly.  Itzhak had two magic lamps, so I decided to
go the 'crystal golem' route and chose a ring of polycontrol and an
amulet of unchanging.  Minetown also had a wand shop that offered
basic charging.  Shortly after returning to the main dungeon I dipped
for Excalibur, which was my primary weapon for most of the game.

On the Mall level, I was attacked by an arc bug and belatedly realized
that I had no MC. BOOM went most of my wands, including polymorph,
which cost me the polyitem conduct and made me a murderer - but it
really wasn't my fault.

Down on DLVL 14, I discovered the bones of Nachtmahr, who died in a
ring shop.  His cursed BoH weighed over 2600, but I was eventually
able to lift it and dip it into holy water.

Deeper in the dungeon, around level 34 IIRC, I came across another
statue of Nachtmahr, whose cursed BoH had within the useful artifacts
of Deluder and Magicbane, as well as silver scales and a blessed
touchstone, all of which I used for the rest of the game.

In Vecna's level, I was hit by a thrown potion of amnesia, but only
forgot the current map - all spells and identifies and main dungeon
maps were unaffected.  That was the only amnesia I had in this game.

I eventually tamed a ki-rin, and equipped it with a shield of
reflection, unicorn horn, +4 gauntlets of dex, and a saddle.  I rode
it around for about half the game. But I didn't have any spare "AoLS
for it, which was unfortunate when it burned itself up on the Plane of
fire.

